  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1108.22 Requirements for All Pool or Spa Components",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1108.22 Requirements for All Pool or Spa Components.\n\n(a) Subject to (b), below, any pool or spa component installed on or after May 1, 2014 including but not limited to filters, filter media, pumps, skimmers, valves, flow meters, suction fittings, chemical feeders, and automatic controllers, shall be:\n\n(1) Certified by NSF or a comparable independent testing organization as meeting applicable NSF/ANSI Standard 50 requirements for the specific use for which it is intended and the specific use conditions to which it will be subject; and\n\n(2) Installed and maintained in accordance with its manufacturer’s instructions.\n\n(b) The owner of a pool or spa that is in operation as of May 1, 2014 may continue to use replaceable parts, such as filter media, that do not meet (a)(1), above, until such time as the component which uses the replaceable parts fails or is otherwise being replaced.\n\nSource. #10577, eff 5-1-14 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100); ss by #13198, eff 5-1-21 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) (formerly Env-Wq 1105.22)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1100.html"
